72
00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:50.500
There are sequential contracts where one
has to finish before the next one starts.

73
00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:54.880
Or you could use a prime contract where
you manage one main supplier and they

74
00:03:54.880 --> 00:03:57.500
handle all the specialist subcontractors
under them.

75
00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:00.000
And the path you choose is a huge
trade-off.

76
00:04:00.500 --> 00:04:04.237
Going with a single supplier usually gets
you preferential rates and makes

77
00:04:04.237 --> 00:04:05.500
communication super easy.

78
00:04:05.500 --> 00:04:09.500
But man, the risk of over-reliance is
